WEBVTT

00:08.501 --> 00:13.351
Thanks to your earrings, I've ascertained
that all is functioning as it should.

00:20.251 --> 00:26.861
Will everyone see things my way 
after we defeat the Jin?

00:33.421 --> 00:37.491
<i>I really have no idea what he's thinking.</i>

00:40.161 --> 00:41.751
The slave girl is gone!

00:41.751 --> 00:44.541
Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:45.131 --> 00:47.711
Did she get lost <i>again</i>?

00:47.711 --> 00:50.201
Lady Möge!

01:00.951 --> 01:03.651
<b>Jaadugar</b>

02:28.641 --> 02:30.131
Hey, Fatima.

02:30.131 --> 02:31.231
Ugh.

02:31.231 --> 02:33.361
So this is where you were.

02:33.901 --> 02:35.981
How dare you run away from me!

02:36.291 --> 02:37.941
Qadaq!

02:37.941 --> 02:39.371
Please help!

02:39.371 --> 02:40.911
Lord Chinqai?

02:39.371 --> 02:40.911
Chinqai?

02:40.911 --> 02:43.541
You can write in Uyghur, yes?

02:49.381 --> 02:51.381
Please take care of these as well.

02:51.381 --> 02:53.131
Is there no end in sight?

02:53.711 --> 02:55.051
I'm sorry about all this.

02:55.451 --> 03:00.001
Everything the Great Kha'an bought 
has to be recorded in our registers.

03:00.981 --> 03:05.441
So why am <i>I</i> here? Isn't this a man's job?

03:05.441 --> 03:07.191
Be quiet and get to work.

03:07.191 --> 03:11.651
Many of the Mongols do not care
for reading and writing.

03:11.651 --> 03:13.921
Thus, we are short on scribes.

03:14.401 --> 03:15.351
Books!

03:16.511 --> 03:18.041
Who will even read these?

03:18.961 --> 03:21.321
This is by Jabir ibn Hayyan.

03:21.321 --> 03:22.021
Huh?

03:23.221 --> 03:24.301
Oh, nothing.

03:31.141 --> 03:34.671
Why is this book hidden away, Mistress?

03:35.421 --> 03:37.811
Oh, this book by Jabir?

03:38.191 --> 03:41.931
Jabir was a man 
who lived in Tus long ago.

03:42.781 --> 03:45.981
But it's not the most reputable of tomes.

03:46.891 --> 03:48.481
What's the subject of his book?

03:51.851 --> 03:53.401
Alchemy.

03:57.081 --> 03:58.491
What's that book about?

03:58.771 --> 04:04.201
It details how one can heat and mix 
various materials such as minerals

04:05.261 --> 04:06.951
to prepare al-iksir.

04:06.951 --> 04:08.541
"Al-iksir"?

04:08.541 --> 04:09.801
What's that?

04:09.801 --> 04:13.171
Something like a cure-all?
Or so I believe.

04:13.171 --> 04:14.921
I'm not too familiar with it.

04:14.921 --> 04:16.481
A cure-all?

04:17.681 --> 04:18.841
Lady Möge.

04:18.841 --> 04:21.801
Do you mean a medicine 
that can cure any ailment?

04:27.241 --> 04:30.851
This is Fatima, my attendant.

04:31.211 --> 04:32.601
Boraqchin Khatun.

04:34.191 --> 04:37.281
<i>So this is the Mongol Empire's
 chief empress.</i>

04:38.441 --> 04:39.701
<i>The Great Khatun.</i>

04:40.491 --> 04:43.991
<i>Why have I been brought to meet her?</i>

04:44.211 --> 04:45.721
Listen to this, Boraqchin.

04:45.721 --> 04:48.201
This girl says she can concoct a cure-all.

04:48.981 --> 04:50.121
You mean danyao?

04:50.121 --> 04:50.991
Huh?

04:51.451 --> 04:56.001
Um, my apologies. I'm not sure
 what all of this is about.

04:56.321 --> 05:00.591
All I said is I can read books
 written in Arabic.

05:00.991 --> 05:02.021
Huh?

05:02.021 --> 05:03.011
Möge.

05:03.011 --> 05:04.561
Oh, but...

05:04.561 --> 05:06.711
That is all. Take your leave.

05:07.551 --> 05:09.481
Sorry for making you come all this way.

05:13.181 --> 05:15.241
What was that about?

05:15.241 --> 05:16.271
Who knows?

05:17.231 --> 05:18.941
Wait!

05:18.941 --> 05:20.151
Lady Möge?

05:20.151 --> 05:23.111
Say, there's something 
I want to discuss with you.

05:23.481 --> 05:25.671
The reason I asked you to come here...

05:27.871 --> 05:28.871
Leave us.

05:32.651 --> 05:35.501
Someone's been administering 
poison to Boraqchin.

05:36.361 --> 05:40.091
You saw how emaciated she was
and how sore-ridden her skin.

05:40.091 --> 05:43.301
Poison? Who's responsible? And why?

05:43.701 --> 05:45.031
I'm not certain.

05:45.391 --> 05:49.541
But I suspect Boraqchin's physician.

05:50.201 --> 05:55.231
Long ago, there was a Daoist doctrine
 known as waidan.

05:55.661 --> 05:56.941
Waidan?

05:56.941 --> 06:03.151
<b>Sandarac</b>

05:56.941 --> 06:03.151
<b>Sulfur</b>

05:56.941 --> 06:03.151
<b>Quicksilver</b>

05:57.331 --> 06:00.601
By combining the likes of sulfur,
 quicksilver, and sandarac,

06:00.601 --> 06:03.591
an elixir called "danyao" can be made.

06:03.971 --> 06:10.911
It was said taking danyao transformed
the body to become immortal like gold.

06:10.911 --> 06:12.191
Is that true?

06:12.191 --> 06:13.511
No.

06:13.511 --> 06:18.171
All who took it succumbed to poison, 
resulting in shortened lifespans.

06:18.551 --> 06:22.751
That is but one reason the practice
 was abandoned long ago.

06:23.471 --> 06:26.551
I'm certain I heard him 
utter the word "poison."

06:26.551 --> 06:29.291
I'm afraid that's not much to go on.

06:29.291 --> 06:32.271
If it worries you so, 
simply keep the physician away.

06:32.271 --> 06:36.461
As Great Khatun, surely it'd be 
a trivial feat to replace him.

06:36.461 --> 06:37.561
Töregene.

06:37.561 --> 06:39.311
Let us return, Fatima.

06:39.311 --> 06:40.701
R-Right.

06:47.571 --> 06:50.661
We shouldn't get involved 
with that eerie woman.

06:51.711 --> 06:53.001
That was harrowing.

06:53.801 --> 06:56.191
Today was the first time 
I'd seen the Great Khatun.

06:56.191 --> 07:00.451
She's a great deal older 
than Emperor Ögedei, isn't she?

07:00.451 --> 07:03.301
Yes. She used to be his stepmother.

07:03.301 --> 07:03.961
What?

07:04.211 --> 07:07.941
Boraqchin and Möge 
were married to Genghis Khan.

07:08.301 --> 07:10.831
Ögedei ended up inheriting them as wives.

07:10.831 --> 07:11.891
Oh?

07:12.331 --> 07:15.771
So those two have known 
each other for a long time.

07:15.771 --> 07:20.601
When the father dies, his wives go
 to his son, except for his birth mother.

07:21.331 --> 07:23.231
It's a common arrangement here.

07:26.491 --> 07:27.741
Boraqchin.

07:30.411 --> 07:34.371
She has no sons, and she doesn't come 
from a particularly large family.

07:35.341 --> 07:40.031
Truth be told, I have no idea 
how she became Great Khatun.

07:43.211 --> 07:49.591
<i>It was said taking danyao transformed
the body to become immortal like gold.</i>

07:50.081 --> 07:52.301
That sounds just like alchemy.

07:52.771 --> 07:55.311
Who knew they had something 
similar in the east?

07:56.191 --> 07:58.271
An immortal body.

07:59.061 --> 08:00.231
You mean danyao?

08:04.141 --> 08:05.441
Could it be?

08:05.951 --> 08:07.631
Al-iksir...

08:08.351 --> 08:11.441
The ingredients are quicksilver, sulfur...

08:12.191 --> 08:14.901
And what else again?

08:18.701 --> 08:20.291
Lady Töregene.

08:20.851 --> 08:23.711
Let us go meet the Great Khatun once more.

08:23.711 --> 08:26.421
Huh? Why?

08:30.441 --> 08:32.551
You have something in mind, don't you?

08:35.021 --> 08:38.381
I'd like you to lend me your power,
 Lady Töregene.

08:42.581 --> 08:47.241
Al-iksir. A wondrous remedy 
that renders one's body immortal.

08:47.241 --> 08:51.571
It lies at the very heart
 of Persian alchemy.

08:51.801 --> 08:55.781
It goes without saying 
that I cannot prepare it by myself.

08:56.221 --> 09:01.041
However, with your help, 
Great Khatun, I could possibly...

09:01.801 --> 09:03.671
Why the talk of this again?

09:04.031 --> 09:07.131
Because it is you 
who has been seeking it.

09:08.121 --> 09:09.461
Am I wrong?

09:10.981 --> 09:12.301
Wait, is that true?

09:12.841 --> 09:16.261
It struck me the moment 
I first laid eyes on you.

09:16.481 --> 09:19.351
If I may surmise 
based on your appearance...

09:20.501 --> 09:23.851
Have you been ingesting rahj al-gar?

09:23.851 --> 09:25.781
Rahj al-gar?

09:27.441 --> 09:29.731
It's a red stone that 
can be found in volcanoes,

09:29.731 --> 09:33.951
and in the east, 
I hear they call it sandarac.

09:35.201 --> 09:36.551
So I was right.

09:37.251 --> 09:42.871
Rahj al-gar is an essential ingredient 
for al-iksir and danyao, after all.

09:43.601 --> 09:46.731
According to the ancient 
physician, Hippocrates,

09:46.731 --> 09:50.511
rahj al-gar <i>does</i> have 
medicinal effects in small doses.

09:50.981 --> 09:51.801
However...

09:52.241 --> 09:54.511
It acts as a poison 
if you continue to take it.

09:55.061 --> 09:59.391
Causing loss of appetite, 
lesions of the skin, and tumors.

09:59.941 --> 10:02.191
Which is what you seem to be suffering.

10:03.171 --> 10:08.731
So you weren't poisoned by anyone?
You chose to ingest that yourself?

10:08.991 --> 10:12.551
Oh, Möge. Is that what you thought?

10:13.291 --> 10:14.951
Fatima, was it?

10:14.951 --> 10:17.591
Take a look inside the drawers
 on that shelf.

10:21.161 --> 10:22.831
Rahj al-gar.

10:23.081 --> 10:25.541
Why were you taking this?

10:29.701 --> 10:32.261
Was it to become immortal?

10:36.801 --> 10:38.181
Yes, that's right.

10:38.181 --> 10:39.891
I'm getting on in age.

10:40.401 --> 10:42.261
I'd like to live a long life.

10:42.261 --> 10:43.601
Boraqchin.

10:44.001 --> 10:47.061
Please ingest some of this, 
Empress Boraqchin.

10:47.631 --> 10:49.551
It's medicine that will cure your poison.

11:01.581 --> 11:03.741
So what <i>is</i> this?

11:03.741 --> 11:04.991
It's a jada stone.

11:04.991 --> 11:06.361
A jada stone?

11:06.361 --> 11:09.001
You're not supposed 
to ingest jada stones.

11:09.001 --> 11:10.381
You're wrong.

11:10.381 --> 11:14.721
It's called a bezoar stone in Persia, 
where it's recognized as an antidote.

11:15.261 --> 11:17.681
You haven't put a curse on this, have you?

11:17.681 --> 11:20.091
Is this the face of someone
 who wishes you ill?

11:32.881 --> 11:36.551
Please summon us here again 
once you've recovered.

11:37.461 --> 11:40.911
I can tell you more 
about the al-iksir then.

11:43.881 --> 11:45.911
Thank you very much.

11:45.911 --> 11:47.881
I haven't done anything.

11:47.881 --> 11:48.921
Surely you jest?

11:49.641 --> 11:53.421
It was only because you were able 
to find me those Persian physicians

11:53.421 --> 11:56.881
that I was able to learn 
of the rahj al-gar.

11:57.641 --> 11:59.451
What will you do about Chagatai?

11:59.451 --> 12:04.181
We were being too hasty by trying 
to suddenly approach Prince Chagatai.

12:04.611 --> 12:08.941
Instead, by earning the trust
 of the Great Khatun,

12:08.941 --> 12:10.951
a path is sure to reveal itself.

12:12.011 --> 12:14.321
A path for both of us.

12:15.121 --> 12:16.321
Yes.

12:17.071 --> 12:18.401
It's just as you say.

12:20.281 --> 12:23.051
<b>Summer, A.D. 1230</b>

12:27.801 --> 12:29.371
<i>Not long after that,</i>

12:30.721 --> 12:35.231
<i>the Mongol emperor embarked 
on an expedition against the Jin dynasty.</i>

12:40.511 --> 12:43.741
<b>Shanxi Region
House of Ögedei Front-Line Camp</b>

12:46.451 --> 12:49.151
You can put those over there.

12:49.151 --> 12:50.201
Möge.

12:51.531 --> 12:52.901
Boraqchin.

12:53.411 --> 12:55.721
You're well enough
 to be walking outside?

12:56.481 --> 12:58.441
Yes, as you can see.

12:58.441 --> 13:00.221
It's all thanks to Fatima.

13:00.221 --> 13:00.991
Right?

13:01.951 --> 13:03.101
Indeed.

13:04.901 --> 13:07.511
I come with a message 
from Empress Boraqchin.

13:07.951 --> 13:11.911
She wishes to speak to Miss Fatima again.

13:15.251 --> 13:20.841
<i>The following year, in order 
to surround the Jin capital, Kaifeng,</i>

13:16.421 --> 13:26.851
<b>Mongols</b>

13:16.421 --> 13:26.851
<b>Southern
Song</b>

13:16.421 --> 13:26.851
<b>Kaifeng</b>

13:16.421 --> 13:26.851
<b>Jin Dynasty</b>

13:20.841 --> 13:24.541
<i>Tolui's army sought permission to 
pass through the lands of Southern Song.</i>

13:25.561 --> 13:26.851
<i>However...</i>

13:27.811 --> 13:29.521
They killed our messenger?

13:29.991 --> 13:32.311
So that's the Southern Song's response?

13:32.901 --> 13:34.271
Do we turn back?

13:35.851 --> 13:36.901
No.

13:37.241 --> 13:39.531
We will proceed south as planned.

13:39.531 --> 13:43.011
We received our reply, 
unfavorable though it may be.

13:43.011 --> 13:47.071
The Southern Song won't take this quietly.

13:49.401 --> 13:50.201
Well...

13:51.081 --> 13:53.401
We will simply defeat
 the Southern Song as well.

14:11.741 --> 14:13.691
<i>Tolui's army breached
 the fortified pass,</i>

14:14.161 --> 14:16.611
<i>then continued along 
perilous mountain roads.</i>

14:19.151 --> 14:22.781
These mountains turned out 
to be no match for us.

14:24.161 --> 14:26.751
The Great Kha'an is sure to be delighted.

14:29.261 --> 14:30.881
You're right.

14:31.701 --> 14:34.841
I know my brother will be overjoyed.

14:44.121 --> 14:45.551
Dear God.

14:46.021 --> 14:48.391
Please watch over Tolui.

14:49.251 --> 14:50.511
Come now.

14:51.131 --> 14:55.481
You know Father would never lose, 
so why bother praying?

14:51.401 --> 14:55.481
<b>Tolui's Son
Hulegu</b>

14:55.481 --> 14:58.651
My word. How can you 
say that before God?

14:59.301 --> 15:02.931
I don't believe Tolui 
would ever lose in battle.

15:03.411 --> 15:04.321
However...

15:04.861 --> 15:07.801
Misfortune can strike 
outside of the battlefield.

15:08.491 --> 15:13.111
Those with too much power 
are viewed with fear and resentment.

15:13.111 --> 15:15.501
Then, you must be careful, too, Mother.

15:15.871 --> 15:17.191
Me?

15:18.251 --> 15:21.341
No one would give me any thought.

15:24.501 --> 15:26.421
I can only hope so.

15:38.111 --> 15:39.591
Hup.

15:45.201 --> 15:46.761
Here you are.

15:46.761 --> 15:48.781
Thank you. Just leave it there.

16:07.021 --> 16:09.241
There. Fresh off the pot.

16:09.241 --> 16:10.861
Thank you very much.

16:11.711 --> 16:14.531
I've brought you some urum,
 Lady Töregene.

16:16.421 --> 16:19.281
I love it the most at this time of year, 
when it's at its ripest.

16:22.861 --> 16:24.151
It's delicious.

16:24.151 --> 16:28.511
Autumn will soon be upon us, 
and the urum will be used to make butter.

16:28.851 --> 16:31.031
This will be the last batch of the season.

16:31.521 --> 16:33.031
Why don't you have some, too?

16:33.031 --> 16:37.541
Oh, I couldn't. Empress Boraqchin 
has actually just summoned me.

16:37.541 --> 16:39.361
Again?

16:39.361 --> 16:42.261
My apologies. I shall be going now.

16:54.251 --> 16:56.301
Fine by me.

17:00.281 --> 17:04.981
In the natural world, 
substance and qualities are intermingled.

17:05.211 --> 17:10.701
One substance can be transformed 
into another by maneuvering its qualities.

17:11.231 --> 17:15.781
In simple terms, that's what this treatise
 by Jabir is talking about.

17:16.531 --> 17:17.741
What's that mean?

17:17.971 --> 17:19.951
By understanding 
the qualities of an object,

17:20.221 --> 17:24.111
one can produce whatever one desires, 
be that a weapon or a remedy.

17:24.111 --> 17:25.671
Wow. That's amazing.

17:25.991 --> 17:27.741
Take sandarac, for example.

17:27.741 --> 17:32.471
Heating rahj al-gar turns it white 
and increases its toxicity.

17:33.011 --> 17:35.631
They approached the truth 
of this world, it seems.

17:35.631 --> 17:39.681
Both the scholars of your homeland 
and the Daoists of the Middle Kingdom.

17:42.561 --> 17:45.221
<i>The Great Kha'an and Empress Boraqchin.</i>

17:45.221 --> 17:48.701
<i>They're thinking about what happens 
after they conquer the Jin.</i>

17:49.491 --> 17:52.201
<i>They're taking a broader view
 of the world.</i>

17:56.441 --> 17:58.331
What's the matter, Fatima?

17:58.631 --> 18:04.291
Well, Lord Chinqai mentioned 
a shortage of scribes.

18:05.011 --> 18:06.361
Why would that be?

18:06.361 --> 18:11.051
Haven't the Mongols obtained people 
and knowledge from all over the world?

18:13.001 --> 18:17.051
It's because most of the intellectuals 
obtained by the Mongols...

18:17.331 --> 18:20.101
now fall under the rule 
of the House of Tolui.

18:20.101 --> 18:21.261
What?

18:21.261 --> 18:25.301
Just like the military, Tolui's house 
is entitled to them as the Otchigin.

18:25.301 --> 18:29.511
Couldn't the Great Kha'an 
just use his authority?

18:29.511 --> 18:32.741
You would have the Great Kha'an 
pilfer his own brother's property?

18:33.721 --> 18:35.011
My apologies.

18:35.841 --> 18:38.661
<i>There's an intellectual imbalance as well?</i>

18:39.621 --> 18:42.621
<i>However, that works to our advantage.</i>

18:43.861 --> 18:46.881
Is that really for the best?

18:48.591 --> 18:50.511
I can't help but feel afraid.

18:50.971 --> 18:54.671
The House of Tolui controls a majority 
in both military and intellectual might.

18:55.391 --> 18:57.111
That only means...

18:57.111 --> 19:00.391
It's even more important to work
in tandem with the House of Tolui.

19:02.011 --> 19:04.561
But does Prince Tolui feel the same way?

19:06.501 --> 19:09.721
Möge. Sorry, but could you leave us?

19:18.121 --> 19:23.371
Until Möge brought you here, 
I have no recollection of ever seeing you.

19:24.021 --> 19:26.161
Who in the world are you?

19:27.221 --> 19:29.421
It's natural you wouldn't
 be familiar with me.

19:32.511 --> 19:36.051
After all, I was serving
 Princess Sorghaghtani.

19:36.971 --> 19:38.651
I urge you to be cautious.

19:38.651 --> 19:41.011
She has not given up on her ambitions.

19:41.261 --> 19:44.051
To see Prince Tolui become 
the Great Kha'an,

19:44.561 --> 19:47.021
and herself the Great Khatun.

19:50.721 --> 19:52.611
Sorghaghtani, you say?

19:54.641 --> 19:58.321
I see. I shall bear it in mind.

19:59.341 --> 20:03.791
But why have you 
divulged this to me, Fatima?

20:04.201 --> 20:07.251
Choose your answer wisely.
 You could pay dearly for it.

20:07.691 --> 20:10.101
<i>It's all right. I can do this.</i>

20:10.521 --> 20:14.671
<i>I have a good idea 
of what's going on in her mind.</i>

20:15.631 --> 20:20.261
Truth be told, I have no idea 
how she became Great Khatun.

20:21.171 --> 20:23.651
<i>No matter how wise 
the Great Khatun may be,</i>

20:23.651 --> 20:28.111
<i>there are surely many who wonder 
the same thing as Lady Töregene.</i>

20:28.651 --> 20:33.151
<i>That's why she surely clings 
to her own acumen.</i>

20:34.171 --> 20:39.071
I have found hope 
in Emperor Ögedei and yourself.

20:40.401 --> 20:46.541
The wisdom you two display 
makes you fit to rule this world.

20:52.031 --> 20:54.711
You truly think so?

20:58.301 --> 21:00.011
But of course.

21:01.881 --> 21:06.751
<i>I expected her to be a crafty one, 
but she was surprisingly easy to handle.</i>

21:07.061 --> 21:09.291
<i>I must report this 
to Lady Töregene at once.</i>

21:09.291 --> 21:11.001
Excuse me!

21:11.711 --> 21:15.251
U-Um, I was making butter.

21:15.251 --> 21:17.611
But I'm still unaccustomed to it.

21:17.611 --> 21:21.071
I have all the milk 
we collected today still left.

21:21.521 --> 21:23.531
Don't worry. I can help.

21:24.601 --> 21:26.441
Thank you so much.

21:29.381 --> 21:31.001
Lady Töregene.

21:32.571 --> 21:33.961
It can wait for later.

21:46.021 --> 21:47.471
Lady Töregene?

21:52.321 --> 21:55.001
There's no need to be
 so nervous, Töregene.

21:56.481 --> 21:59.311
I have something to discuss with you.

22:04.051 --> 22:08.081
<b>Great Khatun Boraqchin</b>

22:14.541 --> 22:18.381
Translation: John K.
Timing: Andy Ellis

22:14.541 --> 22:18.381
